         edges, its side faces, then the front face that shows its value.

         A cube is projected as TossedCube (RollingDie.kt) draws one, through one eye 4 face widths from
         its front plane, and spun, then tilted 20 degrees so its front looks away from the cup's mouth
         from (54,45.5), inside it. The front plane untilted is the die's old size (side 14, or 15 for the 4), and
         each cube's outline is centred on its die's old centre. Spins and centres, in 2-4-5-3-6 order:
         -52 (23,67.5), 28 (30.5,25.9), -5 (56,20.5), 18 (77.6,29.9), and -77 (87,54.2). The side faces
         are the die's real neighbours, whose opposite faces add up to 7. They are shaded by how they
         face the light; the front is not. The dice's paths are generated, with those numbers, by
         scripts/generate-launcher-dice.py: change them there, not here.

